      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Nd(OTf)3 (0.0349 g, 0.05 mmol) in 2.0 mL toluene was added to a suspension of Nd(DBM)3(H2O)2 (0.085 g, 0.1 mmol) in 5.0 mL toluene. The mixture was refluxed for 1 h. The resulting clear solution was filtered and stored at 0 °C overnight, giving yellow crystals. The main text describes the shared route as 2 equiv of Ln(DBM)3(H2O)2 suspended in CH3CN or toluene plus 1 equiv of Ln(OTf)3 under mild heating, isolating the Ln5(DBM)10(OH)5·n(solvent) clusters in about 70% yield.",
